.TH WB\-UPGRADE 1 "" "watchbill"
.SH NAME
wb\-upgrade \- pin the repository to the installed revision
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBwb\fR upgrade [\-\-dry\-run]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Pin the repository to the installed revision: copy its files over .watchbill/revision/, removing those it does not have, and its manifest to .watchbill/revision.sha256, set the lines watchbill: and revision: of watchbill.yml, and add each pattern the installed wb init would write that the file lacks. No other line is changed.
.PP
It says each write first, then writes, runs the check of wb check and says the command that commits the change. It commits nothing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Say the same and write nothing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
It is done and the check holds, or there is nothing to do.
.TP
.B 1
It is refused (a change under .watchbill/ that is not committed, an installed version older than the pinned one) or the check does not hold.
.TP
.B 2
It was used wrongly or the repository is not set up.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wb (1) ,
.BR wb\-check (1) ,
.BR wb\-init (1)
